metadata-generation setup task. `fixTestNativeImageRun` invokes `generatePredefinedCglibProxyClasses`, but that Java task is instrumented by the Native Image agent. Spring then treats the JVM as image code and throws `UnsupportedOperationException: CGLIB runtime enhancement not supported on native image` while trying to generate `ConfigurationClassEnhancerInnerBeanMethodInterceptorTest$CglibProxyConfiguration$$SpringCGLIB$$0`. No `6.0.4` test project, metadata, publication metrics, or dynamic-access coverage was produced.\\n\\nInspect:\\n- `logs/org.springframework:spring-context:6.0.4/native-image-run-fix/fixTestNativeImageRun-2026-10-07T00-54-25-830997Z.log`\\n- `logs/org.springframework:spring-context:6.0.4/library-preparation-preflight/claude-code.log`\\n- `logs/org.springframework:spring-context:6.0.4/library-preparation-preflight/claude-code-session-or9bp1e9.log`\\n\\nManual next steps:\\n1. Reproduce the logged `fixTestNativeImageRun` command and adjust the CGLIB pre-generation task so it runs as a normal JVM process rather than under Native Image agent instrumentation.\\n2. Rerun the `6.0.4` coordinate through metadata generation and the full native test to expose and diagnose the original runtime failure.\\n3. Once tests pass, regenerate and validate metadata, dynamic-access coverage, and execution metrics before publication.\", \"textSignature\": \"{\\\"v\\\":1,\\\"id\\\":\\\"msg_0c80c21d7c1aa0f3016ac598acfe4487d0b1512e7297a21725\\\",\\\"phase\\\":\\\"final_answer\\\"}\"}], \"api\": \"openai-codex-responses\", \"provider\": \"openai-codex\", \"model\": \"gpt-5.6-sol\", \"usage\": {\"input\": 6463, \"output\": 954, \"cacheRead\": 67840, \"cacheWrite\": 0, \"reasoning\": 516, \"totalTokens\": 75257, \"cost\": {\"input\": 0.025852, \"output\": 0.019080000000000003, \"cacheRead\": 0.027136000000000004, \"cacheWrite\": 0, \"total\": 0.07206800000000001}}, \"stopReason\": \"stop\", \"timestamp\": 1791334560478, \"responseId\": \"resp_0c80c21d7c1aa0f3016ac598a11b